# DNA-AND content · life · bacteria (domain Bacteria)
# researched: Pearson biology study guides "Bacteria and Archaea: structure, diversity and roles";
#   prokaryote classification notes; standard microbiology for endospores, biofilms and gene transfer
# Spec: docs/CONTENT-FORMAT.md · wiki/systems/r08-life-sim.md

# ── Shapes ──

@shape coccus
name: Coccus
real: yes
says: a round cell
forms: chains (streptococci), clusters (staphylococci), pairs

@shape bacillus
name: Bacillus
real: yes
says: a rod-shaped cell

@shape spirillum
name: Spirillum
real: yes
says: a stiff spiral cell

@shape spirochete
name: Spirochete
real: yes
says: a flexible corkscrew that twists through liquids

@shape vibrio
name: Vibrio
real: yes
says: a comma-shaped curved rod

# ── Cell parts ──

@part cell-wall
name: Cell wall
real: yes
says: a tough wall around the cell
kinds: gram-positive (thick wall), gram-negative (thin wall plus an outer membrane)

@part flagellum
name: Flagellum
real: yes
says: a spinning whip tail for swimming

@part pili
name: Pili
real: yes
says: hair-like threads for grabbing surfaces and swapping genes

@part capsule
name: Capsule
real: yes
says: a slimy outer coat that protects the cell

@part plasmid
name: Plasmid
real: yes
says: a small ring of extra genes that can be passed to other bacteria

@part endospore
name: Endospore
real: yes
says: a tough sleeping form that survives heat, cold, drying and radiation for years

# ── How they get energy and food ──

@metabolism photoautotroph
name: Light-eater (photoautotroph)
real: yes
says: energy from starlight, carbon from carbon dioxide
example: cyanobacteria

@metabolism chemoautotroph
name: Rock-eater (chemoautotroph)
real: yes
says: energy from chemicals like sulfur, ammonia or iron

@metabolism heterotroph
name: Food-eater (heterotroph)
real: yes
says: eats other living or dead things

@metabolism photoheterotroph
name: Light-and-food user
real: yes
says: energy from light, carbon from food

@oxygen obligate-aerobe
name: Needs oxygen
real: yes

@oxygen obligate-anaerobe
name: Poisoned by oxygen
real: yes

@oxygen facultative
name: Either way
real: yes
says: uses oxygen when it can, switches off when it can't

# ── Main groups (phyla) ──

@phylum proteobacteria
name: Proteobacteria
real: yes
domain: bacteria
example: E. coli, nitrogen fixers

@phylum cyanobacteria
name: Cyanobacteria
real: yes
domain: bacteria
says: the first oxygen makers; built the oxygen air

@phylum firmicutes
name: Firmicutes
real: yes
domain: bacteria
says: soil and gut bacteria, many make endospores

@phylum actinobacteria
name: Actinobacteria
real: yes
domain: bacteria
says: soil bacteria that make many antibiotics

@phylum bacteroidetes
name: Bacteroidetes
real: yes
domain: bacteria
says: gut partners that break down food

@phylum spirochaetes
name: Spirochaetes
real: yes
domain: bacteria
says: corkscrew swimmers

# ── Group life ──

@behavior biofilm
name: Biofilm
real: yes
says: a slimy city of bacteria stuck to a surface, tougher together than alone

@behavior quorum-sensing
name: Quorum sensing
real: yes
says: bacteria count each other by chemical signal and act together once there are enough

@behavior chemotaxis
name: Chemotaxis
real: yes
says: swimming toward food and away from poison

@behavior stromatolite
name: Stromatolite
real: yes
says: layered rock mounds built by mats of bacteria over thousands of years

# ── Swapping genes ──

@genes transformation
name: Transformation
real: yes
says: picking up loose DNA from dead cells

@genes conjugation
name: Conjugation
real: yes
says: passing a plasmid to another bacterium through a pilus

@genes transduction
name: Transduction
real: yes
says: a virus carries genes from one bacterium to another

# ── Generator rules ──

@rule bacteria-fast
real: rule
says: bacteria split in two fast; populations explode when food is there and crash when it runs out

@rule bacteria-gene-swap
real: rule
says: bacteria trade genes sideways, so useful traits like drug resistance spread fast between species

@rule bacteria-everywhere
real: rule
says: bacteria live everywhere life can, from vents to guts, and recycle everything that dies

@rule bacteria-oxygen
real: rule
says: cyanobacteria fill the air with oxygen over time, triggering the great oxidation and poisoning oxygen-hating life

@rule bacteria-partners
real: rule
says: bacteria live inside other life as gut partners, root partners and parasites
